Goliath is a browser automation package for authorized AI-agent workflows.

Dual-use functionality includes an anti-detection Camoufox browser runtime,
persistent authenticated sessions, arbitrary JavaScript evaluation inside pages,
file uploads, cookie import, proxy support, and human-like browser interactions.
These capabilities can resemble security or evasion tooling to automated package
scanners.

The intended legitimate uses are agent-assisted form and document workflows,
accessibility and quality assurance, research, authenticated personal-assistant
tasks, and automation of websites the operator is authorized to access. Goliath
does not grant permission to bypass access controls, violate website terms,
impersonate another person, or access systems or data without authorization.

The package is open source and its network, authentication, telemetry, upload,
and browser-launch behavior can be audited in the published source. Telemetry is
disabled by default, remote binding requires an access key, and uploaded file
paths are confined to an operator-configured directory.
